    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d569">

                <pb facs="0813" n="717" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg717"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Day to Señor Polo de Bernabé.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-03-28"><hi rendition="#italic">March 28,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: I have to acknowledge receipt
                    of your note of 26th instant, informing me that you had telegraphed to H. E. the
                    Governor-General of Cuba, advising him of the arrival at Matanzas of the
                    Norwegian steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Ulstein</hi>, and requesting that all
                    possible facilities and franchises be extended to that vessel, provided the
                    cargo only contains goods for the relief of the reconcentrados.</p>
                <p>Accept my thanks for your courtesy and prompt cooperation in this matter, and
                    believe me,</p>
                <p>Very truly, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William R. Day.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
